    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3ca846a8-5fea-51f0-8b03-1d0b910e047b",
      ":question/problem": "Find $l$, if $5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 51\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 5\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 51\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 51\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $l=2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
